From 0000000000000000000000000000000000000000 Mon Sep 17 00:00:00 2001
From: Dylan Ironside <dylan@dylanironside.io>
Date: Thu, 19 Nov 2026 15:45:14 +0000
Subject: [PATCH] drm/asahi: g16: Map the render notifier records
 ASC-cached by default

Make g16_notifier_cached and g16_lone_ctx_skip default to 1. The render
graph's TA and FS notifier records then live in their own session page
in the ASC-cached class, the attribute index macOS gives its per-queue
objects, and a render with nothing published behind it retires without
the record CONTEXT words, the one host read of that page. The page is
allocated once and never dropped, so no cached mapping is torn down
when a client exits.

Measured on linux-aurora 1.1103 (experimental), one boot with
g16_notifier_cached=1 on the command line against three boots without
it, one reading per cell and boot, in us per submission. The two
values with the word are g16_lone_ctx_skip 0 and 1:

  render.light depth 1:   173.8 -> 163.4, 163.2  (-6.0 %)
  render.light depth 8:    60.0 ->  54.3,  54.4  (-9.5 %)
  render.light depth 64:   59.2 ->  54.8,  54.9  (-7.5 %)
  compute.light depth 1:  150.3 -> 154.8, 152.8
  compute.light depth 8:   33.2 ->  33.2,  32.7
  compute.light depth 64:  19.9 ->  19.5,  19.2

The three boots without the word read render.light 172.9 to 174.3,
59.8 to 60.5 and 58.9 to 59.5, and compute.light 149.8 to 151.0, 32.9
to 33.5 and 19.2 to 20.3.

On that boot a second render.light client was started every 10 s and
stopped after 3 s beside one running at depth 1, three runs of 30 s
with g16_lone_ctx_skip 0 and three with 1: no fault line. Over the
boot 1,324,936 lone proof passes matched their CONTEXT words, none was
held and none needed the skip.

g16_notifier_cached=0 on the kernel command line restores the old
mapping. g16_lone_ctx_skip=0 at run time brings the CONTEXT term back,
and with it a hold that only the completion deadline bounds.

Assisted-by: LLM
---
 drivers/gpu/drm/asahi/asahi_core.rs   |  4 ++--
 drivers/gpu/drm/asahi/g16/lone_ctx.rs |  2 +-
 drivers/gpu/drm/asahi/g16/params.rs   | 14 ++++++++------
 3 files changed, 11 insertions(+), 9 deletions(-)

diff --git a/drivers/gpu/drm/asahi/asahi_core.rs b/drivers/gpu/drm/asahi/asahi_core.rs
index 4567af8db8..0c0a662012 100644
--- a/drivers/gpu/drm/asahi/asahi_core.rs
+++ b/drivers/gpu/drm/asahi/asahi_core.rs
@@ -292,8 +292,8 @@ fn init(module: &'static kernel::ThisModule) -> impl PinInit<Self, Error> {
             description: "G16: 1 queue 2 compute 4 TA 8 FS 16 ring; 32/64/128 work/seq/barrier",
         },
         g16_notifier_cached: u32 {
-            default: 0,
-            description: "G16: 1 = render TA/FS notifier records ASC-cached (default 0; others: 0)",
+            default: 1,
+            description: "G16: 1 = render TA/FS notifier records ASC-cached (default 1; others: 0)",
         },
         g16_render_seq_pool: u32 {
             default: 1,
diff --git a/drivers/gpu/drm/asahi/g16/lone_ctx.rs b/drivers/gpu/drm/asahi/g16/lone_ctx.rs
index 55e80ae5b5..9a1d425a62 100644
--- a/drivers/gpu/drm/asahi/g16/lone_ctx.rs
+++ b/drivers/gpu/drm/asahi/g16/lone_ctx.rs
@@ -6,7 +6,7 @@
 //! The firmware stores the record CONTEXT words at every TA and FS post into the cached line;
 //! they reach memory only when it cleans that line, so the host may read an older value. The
 //! uncached witnesses (firmware and service stamps, queue receipts, pool, scene timestamps)
-//! prove the render as they prove one with work behind it. `g16_lone_ctx_skip` (default 0)
+//! prove the render as they prove one with work behind it. `g16_lone_ctx_skip` (default 1)
 //! drops only the CONTEXT term; at 0 the rule is the old one, case for case.
 
 /// The stats counter a lone proof pass adds to: matched, held back, or retired without CONTEXT.
diff --git a/drivers/gpu/drm/asahi/g16/params.rs b/drivers/gpu/drm/asahi/g16/params.rs
index 80d1a079e5..72def1051f 100644
--- a/drivers/gpu/drm/asahi/g16/params.rs
+++ b/drivers/gpu/drm/asahi/g16/params.rs
@@ -731,7 +731,7 @@ pub(crate) fn fw_cached_mask() -> u32 {
     module_parameters::g16_fw_cached.value()
 }
 
-/// `g16_notifier_cached` (load time, default 0). 1: the render graph's TA and FS notifier
+/// `g16_notifier_cached` (load time, default 1). 1: the render graph's TA and FS notifier
 /// records (the objects the work records name at +0x10 and +0x20) live in their own session
 /// page mapped ASC-cached, the attribute index macOS gives its per-queue objects. The service
 /// stamps the host reads (+0x620, +0x630) and the threshold cells stay in uncached objects.
@@ -3204,15 +3204,17 @@ pub(crate) fn render_work_cached() -> bool {
     "G16: with g16_render_work_pool=1, publish renders with the ASC-cached copy of their unit's work record slot (default 1; 0: the uncached copy; runtime 0644)"
 );
 
-/// Storage of `g16_lone_ctx_skip` (runtime 0644, default 0).
-static LONE_CTX_SKIP: AtomicU32 = AtomicU32::new(0);
+/// Storage of `g16_lone_ctx_skip` (runtime 0644, default 1).
+static LONE_CTX_SKIP: AtomicU32 = AtomicU32::new(1);
 
 /// `g16_lone_ctx_skip`: with `g16_notifier_cached`, 1 = the proof of a render with nothing
 /// published behind it does not need the TA and FS record CONTEXT words, which the host reads
 /// from the ASC-cached record page and so may see before the firmware cleans them. The
 /// uncached stamps, both queue receipts, the pool and the scene timestamps still prove it, as
-/// they prove a render with work behind it. Without `g16_notifier_cached`, or 0 (default): no
-/// change.
+/// they prove a render with work behind it. 1 is the default. At 0 with `g16_notifier_cached`
+/// (the word is writable at run time) such a render is held until the firmware has cleaned its
+/// CONTEXT words, and only the completion deadline bounds that wait. Without
+/// `g16_notifier_cached`: no change.
 pub(crate) fn lone_ctx_skip() -> bool {
     LONE_CTX_SKIP.load(Ordering::Relaxed) == 1 && notifier_cached()
 }
@@ -3223,7 +3225,7 @@ pub(crate) fn lone_ctx_skip() -> bool {
     LONE_CTX_SKIP_PARM,
     LONE_CTX_SKIP,
     "g16_lone_ctx_skip",
-    "G16: 1 = with g16_notifier_cached, retire a render with nothing behind it without the cached record CONTEXT words; stamps, receipts and scene times still prove it (default 0)"
+    "G16: 1 = with g16_notifier_cached, retire a render with nothing behind it without the cached record CONTEXT words; stamps, receipts and scene times still prove it (default 1; 0 holds such a render until its cached CONTEXT words are cleaned)"
 );
 
 /// Storage of `g16_behind_initbm` (runtime 0644, default 1).
-- 
